What is Ferronickel?
Ferronickel is a critical ferroalloy with the CAS number 11110-39-7, characterized as a shiny metallic solid material. It is predominantly produced through the carbothermic reduction of serpentinic minerals, including serpentine, limonite, and garnierite. This essential alloy enables the production of materials with specialized electronic, magnetic, and catalytic properties, making it a cornerstone in various industrial applications. While ferronickel remains stable under normal storage conditions, it poses safety considerations as exposure to carbon oxides in reducing atmospheres can form the toxic gas nickel carbonyl.

